IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mlr-core`
IMPORT `mlr1-reg08-09-application`

-- LAYER 1, regulation 15: the persons and activities the Regulations do not apply to.
-- (Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017.)
-- The text is a plain-text rendering made by a converter script; it is not the official text.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS.  Paragraph (1) lists persons "when carrying on" an activity: the person falling short of the
-- activity is outside the limb's grant (NOTHING: a "when" inside an exclusion, not inside a "means" definition, is left as it was; the reviewer expected JUST FALSE, open question, fork F-leave).  A person who is not of the kind a limb names is
-- not within that limb (JUST FALSE, Marginal readings (e): regulation 8(1)(b) speaks of "the exclusions set out in regulation
-- 15", so the limbs are the whole set).  The seat combines the limbs with `reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions`.

§ `Regulation 15(3) -- Occasional or very limited financial activity`

-- reg 15(3)(a).  The person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity does not exceed £100,000.
-- src:391 | (a) the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity does not exceed £100,000;
@ref reg 15(3)(a) (src:391-391)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 15(3)(a) the turnover limit of 100000 pounds sterling` MEANS 100000

@ref reg 15(3)(a) (src:391-391)
GIVEN `the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(a) the turnover in respect of the financial activity is within the limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity, in pounds sterling` AT MOST `reg 15(3)(a) the turnover limit of 100000 pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all the following conditions are met— (a) the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity does not exceed £100,000" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 15(3)(b).  The financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding £1,000,
-- whether carried out in a single operation or a series of operations which appear to be linked.
-- src:392 | (b) the financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding £1,000, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation, or a series of operations which appear to be linked;
@ref reg 15(3)(b) (src:392-392)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 15(3)(b) the transaction size of 1000 pounds sterling` MEANS 1000

@ref reg 15(3)(b) (src:392-392)
GIVEN `the largest number of transactions exceeding the transaction size that the financial activity involves for any one customer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(b) the financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding 1000 pounds sterling` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the largest number of transactions exceeding the transaction size that the financial activity involves for any one customer` AT MOST 1 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) the financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding £1,000" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 15(3)(c).  The financial activity does not exceed 5% of the person's total annual turnover.
-- src:393 | (c) the financial activity does not exceed 5% of the person's total annual turnover;
@ref reg 15(3)(c) (src:393-393)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 15(3)(c) the share of 5 per cent` MEANS 5

@ref reg 15(3)(c) (src:393-393)
GIVEN `the person's annual turnover from the financial activity, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's total annual turnover, in pounds sterling` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(c) the financial activity does not exceed 5 per cent of the person's total annual turnover` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person's annual turnover from the financial activity, in pounds sterling` TIMES 100 AT MOST `reg 15(3)(c) the share of 5 per cent` TIMES `the person's total annual turnover, in pounds sterling` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the financial activity does not exceed 5% of the person's total annual turnover" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 15(3)(d).  The financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity.
-- A judgement the text leaves to whoever applies it: an input.
-- src:394 | (d) the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity;
@ref reg 15(3)(d) (src:394-394)
GIVEN `the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(d) the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 15(3)(e).  The financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means.
-- src:395 | (e) the financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means;
@ref reg 15(3)(e) (src:395-395)
GIVEN `the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money, or any representation of monetary value, by any means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(e) the financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the financial activity is the transmission or remittance of money, or any representation of monetary value, by any means` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(e) the financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- reg 15(3)(f).  The person's main activity is not that of a person falling within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k).
-- Regulation 8(2)(g) is high value dealers; the other ten letters name the other fourteen listed kinds (c names four).
-- An auction platform is not on the list in regulation 8(2) (see `reg 8(2)` in module 1), so it is not within (a) to (f) or (h) to (k).
-- src:396 | (f) the person's main activity is not that of a person falling within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k);
@ref reg 15(3)(f) (src:396-396)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(f) the kind of main activity falls within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `credit institution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `financial institution` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `auditor` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `insolvency practitioner` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `external accountant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `tax adviser` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `independent legal professional` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `trust or company service provider` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `estate agent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `letting agent` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `high value dealer` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)" (letter (g), high value dealers, lies between the two ranges and is in neither)
    WHEN `casino` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `art market participant` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `cryptoasset exchange provider` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `custodian wallet provider` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `auction platform` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): an auction platform is not listed in regulation 8(2), so the letters (a) to (f) and (h) to (k) say nothing of it

@ref reg 15(3)(f) (src:396-396)
GIVEN `the kinds of the person's main activity` IS A LIST OF `Kind of relevant person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(f) the person's main activity is not that of a person falling within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF any (GIVEN k YIELD `reg 15(3)(f) the kind of main activity falls within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)` k EQUALS JUST TRUE) `the kinds of the person's main activity` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(f) the person's main activity is not that of a person falling within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")
        IF all (GIVEN k YIELD `reg 15(3)(f) the kind of main activity falls within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k)` k EQUALS JUST FALSE) `the kinds of the person's main activity` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): a kind of main activity that regulation 8(2) does not list is not shown to fall within, or outside, letters (a) to (f) and (h) to (k)

-- reg 15(3)(g).  The financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person and is not offered to the public.
-- src:397 | (g) the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person and is not offered to the public.
@ref reg 15(3)(g) (src:397-397)
GIVEN `the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the financial activity is offered to the public` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3)(g) the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity and is not offered to the public` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person` AND (NOT (`the financial activity is offered to the public`)) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(g) the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person and is not offered to the public" (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if")

-- reg 15(3).  A person is to be considered as engaging in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis if all the
-- conditions (a) to (g) are met.
-- src:390 | (3) For the purposes of paragraphs (1)(f) and (2), a person is to be considered as engaging in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis if all the following conditions are met—
-- src:391 | (a) the person's total annual turnover in respect of the financial activity does not exceed £100,000;
-- src:392 | (b) the financial activity is limited in relation to any customer to no more than one transaction exceeding £1,000, whether the transaction is carried out in a single operation, or a series of operations which appear to be linked;
-- src:393 | (c) the financial activity does not exceed 5% of the person's total annual turnover;
-- src:394 | (d) the financial activity is ancillary and directly related to the person's main activity;
-- src:395 | (e) the financial activity is not the transmission or remittance of money (or any representation of monetary value) by any means;
-- src:396 | (f) the person's main activity is not that of a person falling within regulation 8(2)(a) to (f) or (h) to (k);
-- src:397 | (g) the financial activity is provided only to customers of the main activity of the person and is not offered to the public.
@ref reg 15(3) (src:390-397)
GIVEN `the answers for conditions (3)(a) to (3)(g)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(3) the person engages in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis` MEANS
    `reg 8(1) all of the conditions of the list hold` `the answers for conditions (3)(a) to (3)(g)`

§ `Regulation 15(1) and (2) -- Persons to whom Parts 1 to 4, 6 and 8 to 11 do not apply`

-- reg 15(1)(a).  A registered society within the meaning of section 1 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act
-- 2014, when it issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of that Act, or accepts deposits from the
-- public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act.
-- src:377 | (1) Parts 1 to 4, 6 and 8 to 11 do not apply to the following persons when carrying on any of the following activities—
-- src:378 | (a) a registered society within the meaning of section 1 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014 (meaning of “registered society”) , when it—
-- src:379 | (i) issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of that Act (maximum shareholding in society); or
-- src:380 | (ii) accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act (carrying on of banking by societies);
@ref reg 15(1)(a) (src:377-380)
GIVEN `the person is a registered society within the meaning of section 1 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1)(a) the Parts do not apply to the registered society` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a registered society within the meaning of section 1 of the Co-operative and Community Benefit Societies Act 2014`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15" (regulation 8(1)(b); Marginal readings, (e): the limbs of regulation 15 are the whole set)
        IF `it issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 24 of that Act` OR `it accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 67(2) of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when it— (i) issues withdrawable share capital within the limit ...; or (ii) accepts deposits from the public within the limit ..." (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

