      `it issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 6 of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 7(3) of that Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1)(b) the Parts do not apply to the society registered in Northern Ireland` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is a society registered under the Industrial and Provident Societies Act (Northern Ireland) 1969`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15" (regulation 8(1)(b); Marginal readings, (e): the limbs of regulation 15 are the whole set)
        IF `it issues withdrawable share capital within the limit set by section 6 of that Act` OR `it accepts deposits from the public within the limit set by section 7(3) of that Act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when it— (i) issues withdrawable share capital within the limit ...; or (ii) accepts deposits from the public within the limit ..." (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

-- reg 15(1)(c).  A person who is (or falls within a class of persons) specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38, 40 to 49
-- or 58 of the Schedule to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Exemption) Order 2001, when carrying out any activity in
-- respect of which that person is exempt.
-- src:384 | (c) a person who is (or falls within a class of persons) specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38 , 40 to 49 or 58 of the Schedule to the Financial Services and Markets Act 2000 (Exemption) Order 2001 , when carrying out any activity in respect of which that person is exempt;
@ref reg 15(1)(c) (src:384-384)
GIVEN `the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1)(c) the paragraph of the Schedule is one of those named` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (`the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` AT LEAST 2 AND `the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` AT MOST 23) OR (`the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` AT LEAST 26 AND `the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` AT MOST 38) OR (`the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` AT LEAST 40 AND `the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` AT MOST 49) OR `the number of the paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order that specifies the person` EQUALS 58 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38, 40 to 49 or 58" (a paragraph outside those ranges is not named)

@ref reg 15(1)(c) (src:384-384)
GIVEN `the person is, or falls within a class of persons, specified in a paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that paragraph is one of those named in regulation 15(1)(c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `it is carrying out an activity in respect of which it is exempt` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1)(c) the Parts do not apply to the person specified in the Exemption Order` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is, or falls within a class of persons, specified in a paragraph of the Schedule to the Exemption Order`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not come within the exclusions set out in regulation 15" (regulation 8(1)(b); Marginal readings, (e): the limbs of regulation 15 are the whole set)
        IF `that paragraph is one of those named in regulation 15(1)(c)` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "specified in any of paragraphs 2 to 23, 26 to 38, 40 to 49 or 58"
        IF `that paragraph is one of those named in regulation 15(1)(c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE AND `it is carrying out an activity in respect of which it is exempt` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "when carrying out any activity in respect of which that person is exempt" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)

