-- reg 15(1).  The Parts that do not apply: Parts 1 to 4, 6 and 8 to 11.  Parts 5 and 7 are not named: the paragraph is silent
-- about them.  (The seat asks this of one Part at a time.)  Fork F-15(1): regulation 8(1)(b) takes a person who comes within regulation 15 out of
-- "relevant persons" for every Part, while paragraph (1) names only Parts 1 to 4, 6 and 8 to 11; both are encoded as the text has them (NOTES, fork register).
-- src:377 | (1) Parts 1 to 4, 6 and 8 to 11 do not apply to the following persons when carrying on any of the following activities—
@ref reg 15(1) (src:377-377)
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(1) the Part is one of those that do not apply` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (part AT LEAST 1 AND part AT MOST 4) OR part EQUALS 6 OR (part AT LEAST 8 AND part AT MOST 11) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names "Parts 1 to 4, 6 and 8 to 11" and says nothing of any other Part

-- reg 15(2).  These Regulations do not apply to a person who falls within regulation 8 solely as a result of that person engaging in
-- financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis as set out in paragraph (3).
-- src:389 | (2) These Regulations do not apply to a person who falls within regulation 8 solely as a result of that person engaging in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis as set out in paragraph (3).
@ref reg 15(2) (src:389-389)
GIVEN `the person falls within regulation 8 solely as a result of the financial activity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reg 15(3) the person engages in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(2) the Regulations do not apply to the person who falls within regulation 8 solely as a result of financial activity` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person falls within regulation 8 solely as a result of the financial activity`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "solely as a result of that person engaging in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis"
        IF `reg 15(3) the person engages in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `reg 15(3) the person engages in financial activity on an occasional or very limited basis` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "as set out in paragraph (3)": paragraph (3) counts the activity as occasional or very limited "if all the following conditions are met", and they are not (Marginal readings, (a): a failed condition of an "if"; the answer of reg 15(3) is passed through)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): paragraph (3) has not answered whether its conditions are met

§ `Regulation 15(4) -- Bodies to which Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 2, and Parts 3 to 9, do not apply`

-- reg 15(4).  The bodies.
DECLARE `reg 15(4) body` IS ONE OF
