-- src:403 | (e) the Comptroller and Auditor General for Northern Ireland;
-- src:404 | (f) the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court, when acting as trustee in his or her official capacity;
-- src:405 | (g) the Treasury Solicitor.
@ref reg 15(4) (src:398-405)
GIVEN body IS A `reg 15(4) body`
      `the Official Solicitor is acting as trustee in his or her official capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(4) the Chapters and Parts do not apply to the body` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF body EQUALS `reg 15(4)(f) the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court` AND (NOT (`the Official Solicitor is acting as trustee in his or her official capacity`)) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Official Solicitor to the Supreme Court, when acting as trustee in his or her official capacity" (LEAVE: reviewer expected JUST FALSE; open question, fork F-leave)
        IF body EQUALS `reg 15(4) another body` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "do not apply to— (a) ... (g)" (Marginal readings, (e): the limbs of regulation 15 are the whole set)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- reg 15(4).  The Chapters and Parts: Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 2, and Parts 3 to 9.  Other Parts and Chapters are not named.
@ref reg 15(4) (src:398-398)
GIVEN part IS A NUMBER
      chapter IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15(4) the Chapter of the Part is one of those that do not apply to the bodies` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF part EQUALS 2 AND (chapter EQUALS 2 OR chapter EQUALS 3) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF part AT LEAST 3 AND part AT MOST 9 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the paragraph names "Chapters 2 and 3 of Part 2, and Parts 3 to 9" and says nothing of any other Part or Chapter

§ `Regulation 15 -- The person comes within the exclusions (answers regulation 8(1)(b))`

-- reg 8(1)(b) asks whether the person comes within the exclusions set out in regulation 15.  This gathers the limbs of regulation 15
-- by hand (ruling E1, option B: guidance for gathering by hand); each limb has its own answer above (option C).
-- Any limb that holds answers JUST TRUE; if every limb answers JUST FALSE the person is in none of them (Marginal readings, (e));
-- anything else is NOTHING.  Paragraph (2)'s answer joins the others.
-- src:376 | 15 Exclusions
@ref reg 15 (src:376-376)
GIVEN `the answers for paragraphs (1)(a) to (1)(g), (2) and (4)` IS A LIST OF MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`reg 15 the person comes within the exclusions` MEANS
    `reg 8(2) one of the limbs of the list holds` `the answers for paragraphs (1)(a) to (1)(g), (2) and (4)`

